// Case studies (user request, 2026-09-29): real North Pacific events of the
// past year, walked through step by step in the Past year viewer. Each step
// sets the map (the Past year's view, anomaly or value, lines and wind), opens
// its day, points the camera, and optionally pins the probe or offers to play
// a run of days; its text says what to look at and why.
//
// Every number in the texts comes from the archive's own GFS analyses (the
// 00 UTC analysis of the day named, 1 degree grid) unless the text credits
// another source; sources are listed per case. The archive rolls forward a
// day at a time, so a case whose days have left it is shown as no longer
// available rather than opened on the wrong days.
//
// Pure, no imports: node --test loads it. The texts are HTML (trusted: they're
// written here, not taken from data).

// A case: {id, region (pnw | hawaii | pacific, the list's groups), title, when,
// where, summary, sources, steps}. A step: {title, text, why (why this map), lookFor (what to find on it), day: "YYYY-MM-DD", show: {view, mode, lines, wind,
// windAs}, look: {lat, lon, span (deg of latitude in view), tilt (deg from
// straight down, 0-60)}, probe: [lat, lon] | undefined, play: [fromDay,
// toDay] | undefined, marks: [{lat, lon, label, r km}] (rings and labels on
// the map at the features the text names) | undefined}.
const P = (view, mode = "actual", lines = "auto", wind = "auto", windAs = "flow") => ({ view, mode, lines, wind, windAs });

